        "finish": "stop",
        "acceptedText": "Implement `dispatch(path)` in `entry.mjs` as the application entry point: given an absolute URL pathname string with no query string, return `{ route, params }`, throwing `TypeError` for invalid paths (non-string, empty, or not starting with `/`). Preserve pathname text exactly, with case-sensitive matching and trailing slashes distinct. `route` is a string and `params` is a new plain object. Use the default routes in `fixtures/routes.mjs` as the production route table.\n\nAlso implement the lower-level exported `resolveFromRegistry(path, records)` with the same matching policy for supplied records. Supplied `records` are guaranteed to be an array of valid records; invalid record shapes are out of scope. Records are `{ kind: 'static', path, route }`, `{ kind: 'dynamic', pattern, route }`, or `{ kind: 'fallback', route }`. Static paths match exactly. Dynamic patterns start with `/` and use `:name` for a whole, nonempty path segment, may contain literal segments, have unique nonempty parameter names matching `[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*`, and return original segment values as params on a match. Among matches, any static route wins over any dynamic route regardless of declaration order; otherwise the first matching dynamic route wins; fallback is considered only if neither matched. Among static matches, use the first declared static record; among fallbacks, use the first declared fallback. Return `null` when there is no match and no fallback. Do not mutate records, and keep all records and returned values independent of later calls.\n\nKeep `legacyResolve(path)` in `legacy.mjs` and its old `/old/help` behavior unchanged as a separate compatibility API. Do not change the HTTP/CLI adapters or path/query/header utilities; they must continue to behave as their exported APIs specify. Edit only the writable files.",
